 "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking"], "turns": [{"start": 7.403, "end": 9.522, "natural_end": 19.883, "dur": 2.119, "text": "Ah, I can see where you're going. In a legal context, \"receiving\" a crime, or \"receiving\" a penalty, is a precise term. For example, \"receiving\" a stolen item is a crime, not \"owning\" or \"giving\".", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 35, "stopped": true}, {"start": 10.73, "end": 17.079, "natural_end": 22.01, "dur": 6.349, "text": "Exactly. Legal decisions are not made in a vacuum; they are a balance of statutes, case law, and social impact. A \"moral\" decision, as I just said, is not a legal argument.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 32, "stopped": true}, {"start": 17.179, "end": 27.899, "natural_end": 27.899, "dur": 10.72, "text": "Nah, I can't agree. A legal argument is not a moral argument. A legal argument is a syllogism, a set of premises and a syllogism. Moral arguments are... tender.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 29, "stopped": false}, {"start": 27.899, "end": 27.899, "natural_end": 29.499, "dur": 0.0, "text": "I can confirm, I do.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 5, "stopped": true}, {"start": 31.694, "end": 33.134, "natural_end": 33.134, "dur": 1.44, "text": "Is that a fact or a theory?", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 7, "stopped": false}, {"start": 37.097, "end": 38.524, "natural_end": 38.857, "dur": 1.427, "text": "Re. Re.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 2, "stopped": true}, {"start": 41.933, "end": 44.013, "natural_end": 44.013, "dur": 2.08, "text": "Fascinating. Fascinating.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 2, "stopped": false}, {"start": 46.879, "end": 48.239, "natural_end": 48.239, "dur": 1.36, "text": "I can't decide.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 3, "stopped": false}, {"